00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:52.680
most liquid names. The smartest retail investors I know never use pure market orders on stocks with

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:58.140
average daily volume under 1 million shares. Instead, they use limit orders placed intelligently

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.800
between the current bid and ask, or they simply wait for the first 15 minutes of trading

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:08.480
when spreads are typically at their widest to pass before entering. The biggest misconception

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:12.940
among newer investors is believing that the last traded price you see on your screen is guaranteed

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:18.080
to be the price you will actually receive. In reality, you should always check the current bid-ask

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:23.580
